gambatte-pico patch to upstream gambatte (libgambatte/src/video.cpp), GPL-2.0 like the file it
changes. Copyright (c) 2026 TheGammaSqueeze. Applied by build.sh to a copy in out/src.

A save state of an original Game Boy (DMG) game carried 24 bytes nobody wrote: the CGB colour
palette field is only filled for colour games, so the rest of the state was whatever the stack
held there. Two consoles saving the same game state got different bytes, and the netplay check,
which compares the consoles' states, saw them part although the games were identical. The field
is now cleared for DMG games (it is only read back for colour ones).

diff -ruN a/libgambatte/src/video.cpp b/libgambatte/src/video.cpp
--- a/libgambatte/src/video.cpp	2026-11-16 21:35:58.061156228 +0000
+++ b/libgambatte/src/video.cpp	2026-11-16 21:35:58.083156228 +0000
@@ -87,6 +87,8 @@
    
    if (isCgb())
       std::memcpy(state.ppu.dmgPalette, dmgColorsGBC_, 8 * 3);
+   else
+      std::memset(state.ppu.dmgPalette, 0, 8 * 3);
    
 
    lycIrq_.saveState(state);
